// Custom event schema declaring a group whose name is NEITHER `input` NOR
// `output`: `meta` is a named record group with a `region` member, addressed
// as `meta.region`.
//
// NOTE on scope: the dwschema spread selectors (`...inputs(A)` / `...outputs(A)`)
// are fixed to the group names `input` / `output` by construction (they splice
// the action's `context.input` / `context.output` records), so a spread cannot
// be re-homed under a differently-named group. What the surface DOES support —
// and what this case exercises — is an author-declared *named record* group
// with an arbitrary name (the same mechanism `__drupe` uses in 1123).
// This is the substance of "a group other than input/output": the compiler and
// encoder must resolve `meta.region` by its dotted path, with no hardcoded
// assumption that the only groups are `input`/`output`.

decision event <A>::request {
    ...inputs(A),
    callerPrincipal: principalType(A),
    callerResource:  resourceType(A),
    requestId:       String,
    meta:              { region: String },
}

event <A>::response {
    ...inputs(A),
    ...outputs(A),
    callerPrincipal: principalType(A),
    callerResource:  resourceType(A),
    requestId:       String,
    meta:              { region: String },
}
